# Nintendo News Center 🎮

A macOS menu bar app that notifies you about the latest Nintendo news, with notifications translated into Spanish, English, Catalan and German.

## Features

- Menu bar icon with the Switch logo.
- Automatic news check every 30 minutes (RSS feed from [Nintenderos](https://www.nintenderos.com)).
- Native macOS notifications with the headline of each news item.
- Headline translation into 4 languages (es, en, cat, de).
- Menu with:
  - Search news now.
  - Saved news counter.
  - Clear history.
  - Open the news website.
  - Latest news headline.
  - Language selector.
  - Keyword filter (for example, "switch 2" or "mario"), with the option to add your own keywords.

## Requirements

- macOS
- Python 3.10 or newer

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/pet-on-menu-bar.git
cd pet-on-menu-bar
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install pystray pillow feedparser deep-translator psutil pyobjc
python terra.py
```

## Files

- `terra.py`: main program.
- `pet_feliz.png`, `pet_cansado.png`: icons (optional; a default icon is used if they are missing).
- `palabras_clave.json`: keywords used to filter news. If the list is empty, all news is shown.
- `noticias_vistas.json`: history generated automatically.

## Example `palabras_clave.json`

```json
["switch 2", "mario"]
```

## Known limitations

- On macOS, the menu text only updates when you open the menu again.
- Translation uses Google Translate without an API key. If too many requests are sent in a row, it may fail and the original headline is shown.
- Notifications use `osascript`, so you need to allow them in System Settings.

